# Hama, the Bloodbender: "for as long as you control Hama" (CR 611.2b). Bot1 exiles Bot2's Shock with Hama, and Bot2 takes Hama with Act of
# Treason on turn 2. The permission was Bot1's and Bot1 no longer controls Hama, while Bot2, who never was "you", has none: Bot2 may not cast the
# Shock in its own turn although Mox Ruby is untapped and it controls Hama. The duration ended for good: when Hama goes back to Bot1 at end of
# turn, Bot1 may not cast the Shock either, though Mox Jet is untapped.

